[h1]Life Framework: Everon 1989[/h1]

DRAFT, not yet signed off.

Everon, 1989. You have just arrived in a village where everyone knows everyone and nobody has told you the rules. You fill in form R-89, collect an ID card from the clerk on the square and find your feet. Honest work pays: parcels, fuel, fares. The bank keeps your money and the police keep order. At the edge of the village a few people make more on a good night than on a good week, and the police would like a word.

This is the flagship content pack for [b]Life Framework (Core)[/b], an open-source roleplay framework for Arma Reforger. The core is pulled in when you subscribe, so you need nothing else. It is unfinished: you will find rough edges and things that change between versions.

[h2]How to play[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to this item.
[*]Solo: open [b]Scenarios[/b], pick [b]Life Framework: Everon 1989[/b] and press Play.
[*]With friends: one of you hosts it from the Scenarios list, or joins a server that runs it.
[/list]

[h2]What to try[/h2]
[list]
[*]Fill in form R-89 when you arrive, then talk to the clerk on the square for your ID card.
[*]Take the parcel job at the depot. Fuel delivery and the taxi open as you level up.
[*]Bank your pay at the ATM and buy food at the general store.
[*]Collect your car from the garage, get the other one out of the impound, or buy one at the car lot.
[*]Rob a till, drill the bank vault or the cash van, and see the police get the call.
[*]Clock in at the police desk, work the wanted board, fine and jail.
[*]Get hurt and wait for the medic, or give up and respawn.
[*]Found an organization, use the hideout stash, sell to the fence, and run the moonshine still.
[/list]

[h2]Playtest settings[/h2]
[list]
[*]Your cash and bank top up when they run low, so you can try everything without grinding.
[*]Every new character owns two test cars, one in the garage and one at the impound.
[*]The first player on a server with no police is put on the police roster.
[*]Progress is saved and carries over a server restart.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Life Framework (Core), version 0.1.0 or later. Subscribing to this item pulls it in.
[*]Arma Reforger.
[/list]

